A||||7||fierospeeder||Day time running lights||||13||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||11-30-1999||01:43 AM||||Anyone else besides me hate the idea of day time running lights?  I understand the point which is suppose to help the driver in another vehicle to see you.  But is that necessary in the day time?  I've seen drivers, who have late model cars that were never equipped with day time running lights, and they would turn on their headlights.  One time i wasn't able to see the uncoming vehicle because maybe they were using their brights for day time running lights.  Parking lights are fine, but having headlights behind you is a pain, just like those suvs tailgating you because they can stop really quick!  Motorcycles are fine with their lights on.  Anyone else hate seeing headlights, and "poseurs" making you put your sunglasses on?  ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-30-1999||01:28 PM||||I drove a truck for 15 years so I can honestly say that daytime running lites make a HUGE difference in visibility.  Not necessarily on the highway in sunny weather, but think of all of the idiots who refuse to turn on ANY lights at dusk or dawn or in the rain, etc.  I think that daytime running lites are even more important for us because we aren't very visible (49" tall isn't much!).  BTW, I don't like them.  I never thought they looked good. But, when I get my car finished (OK...IF I get it finished!), I will have them.  I plan on adding a chin spoiler and integrating driving lites into it.  I'll try to get colored lites (amber is ugly, but most laws won't let you have anything else.), and I'll make them small, but they will be on all the time.  I'll get off my soapbox now.  Thank you and please vote for me.;-)||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||11-30-1999||02:47 PM||||In Illinois, it is the law to turn on your headlights while your windshield wipers are being used.  I'm not sure how much it is enforced because i see people who dont have their lights on at all.  Another thing is people who havn't changed their brake lights and its like nascar, you have to figure out when they are stopping before you go right into them. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||11-30-1999||03:35 PM||||I personally like the new corvettes day time running lights. (Firebird too). I don't like any others. Now I'm wondering why its illegal to have fog lights on during the day without the headlights on. I know a person who got pulled over for this and just said he forgot to turn them off. Then the cop told him that they have to be connected to the low beam circuit and gave him a ticket for it. Since when were fog lights called OFF-ROAD LAMPS??????????||||reg||1
Z||000004||olympic||11-30-1999||04:16 PM||||Here in Canada, daytime running lights have been mandatory on all cars since 1992. Most cars turn on the hi beams when you turn on the key. They just supply a lower voltage so that the headlight is very visible but not blinding. Some top line cars even have a photosensitive "eye" in the dash that automatically swith the headlight from daytime running lights to low beams when it gets dark. The Grand Marquis is one of them, you never have to pull the headlight switch on or turn them off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RZURCTN||11-30-1999||08:32 PM||||My 96 Grand Am does the same thing.  But I think there is something wrong with it as it has no day time running lamps.  If the lo beams aren't on (either automaticly or manualy) then there are no lights on.  I'd like to have day time running lamps for my Fiero.  Anyone know where to get them or how to rearrange the wiring to make it work?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||11-30-1999||09:07 PM||||I've been told that in order to have driving/fog lights, you need to wire them so that they can only be turned on if the headlights or parking lights are on with them. Sounds pretty dorky to me, and if I were to ever put them on one of my cars, I'd wire them any way I wanted to.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-01-1999||02:46 AM||||Fierospeeder--that's the law in a few other states, too.  I've talked to people who have been pulled over in NY for that.<P>Formula--I will design mine after the Firebirds, too.  That's one of the best looking ways to do it.<P>Olympic--You guys gotta have 2 outside rear view mirrors, too.  You guys get all the cool rules.  (OK...some of them suck)<P>Fiero56--I don't know if there are any laws to that effect, but it makes sense.  Most new cars are wired that way so it will be less likely to leave any lights on and drain your battery.||||reg||1
